<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | OurGarage"
  description="What OurGarage collects (nothing, unless you choose to share a garage), where shared data is stored, and how to have it deleted."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="wrap prose legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 15 November 2026</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>If you use OurGarage without an account, we collect nothing. Not your email,
    not your car, not analytics, not a crash report. Your garage lives in a
    database file on your phone and never reaches us.</p>
    <p>You only get an account if you choose to share a garage with your household.
    That is the only thing that sends any data anywhere, and we only ask for it at
    the moment you tap &ldquo;Share with household.&rdquo;</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>OurGarage is made by Nokta Studio. Contact: <strong>support@noktastudio.dev</strong></p>

    <h2>What we collect, and only when</h2>

    <h3>Using the app without an account</h3>
    <p>Nothing. OurGarage contains no analytics SDK, no crash reporting SDK, and no
    advertising SDK, and makes no network request carrying your data. Your
    vehicles, service history, reminders, odometer readings, costs and notes are
    stored only in a local database on your device.</p>
    <p>You can use OurGarage this way indefinitely. It is not a trial, and no feature
    of the free, local-only tier stops working after any period of time.</p>

    <h3>If you create an account to share a garage</h3>
    <p>An account is requested only when you choose to share a garage with your
    household — never on first launch, never in the background. Signing in uses
    <strong>Sign in with Apple</strong>, the only sign-in method OurGarage offers. At that point
    we receive and store:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your email address</strong>, from Sign in with Apple. If you choose Apple's Hide
      My Email option, we receive a private relay address and never see your real
      one.</li>
      <li><strong>Your display name</strong>, if Apple provides it. Apple sends this only on the
      very first authorization between you and this app, and only if you agree to
      share it. We use it to name your household by default (for example,
      &ldquo;Fatih's garage&rdquo;). If it is withheld, your household is simply called &ldquo;My
      household,&rdquo; and nothing else about the app changes.</li>
      <li><strong>A user identifier</strong>, generated by our backend provider (Supabase) to
      represent your account, and shared with our payments provider (RevenueCat)
      so a purchase can be matched to the household it should unlock.</li>
      <li><strong>Your garage data</strong> — vehicles, service records, reminder rules, odometer
      readings, costs, and notes — uploaded to our servers so the people in your
      household can see the same information on their own devices. Data you enter
      before joining or creating a household is never uploaded unless and until
      you take that action.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>If you buy OurGarage Premium</h3>
    <p>Purchases are handled entirely by Apple through StoreKit, using our payments
    provider, RevenueCat, to determine which product you bought and whether your
    entitlement is currently active. This is how we know which Premium features
    to unlock. <strong>We never receive your card number, billing
    address, or any other payment details — Apple does not share these with us or
    with RevenueCat.</strong></p>

    <h2>What we never do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not track you across other companies' apps or websites.</li>
      <li>We do not use any advertising, analytics, or crash-reporting SDK of any
      kind, in either the free or the account-based tier.</li>
      <li>We do not show the App Tracking Transparency prompt, because we do not do
      anything that requires it — there is no <code>NSUserTrackingUsageDescription</code> in
      this app for that reason.</li>
      <li>We do not sell your data, and we do not share it with data brokers or
      advertisers.</li>
      <li>We do not send marketing email. There is no mailing list.</li>
      <li>We do not read your location, your contacts, your photos, or your browsing
      history. OurGarage never asks for any of these permissions.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who can see your garage</h2>
    <p>Only the people in your household. Access to shared data is enforced on our
    servers, per household, using row-level security — not merely hidden by the
    app's interface — so another OurGarage user cannot see your garage even if
    they tried to access it directly.</p>
    <p>Invite codes expire seven days after they are created and can be redeemed
    once. Managing invites and members from within the app is coming in an
    upcoming update. Until then, if you want a pending invite revoked or a member
    removed from your household, email <strong>support@noktastudio.dev</strong> and we will
    do it for you.</p>
    <p>Removing a member from a household ends that person's access to it. It does
    <strong>not</strong> delete the vehicles or service history they could see — that data
    belongs to the household as a whole, and deleting it because one person left
    would destroy records the remaining members still rely on.</p>

    <h2>Where your data is stored</h2>
    <p>Data from the free, local-only tier is stored exclusively on your device and
    nowhere else.</p>
    <p>If you use household sharing, your garage data, email address, and display
    name are additionally stored on infrastructure operated by Supabase, our
    backend provider, and referenced by RevenueCat, our payments provider, for the
    purposes described above. Both act as processors of your data on our behalf
    and are contractually restricted from using it for their own purposes.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep your data, and how to delete it</h2>
    <p>We keep account data for as long as you have an account, and delete it
    when you delete your account.</p>
    <p><strong>You can delete your account inside the app:</strong> Settings &rarr;
    <strong>Delete account</strong>. The option appears once you have signed in. To confirm,
    you sign in with Apple once more. Deleting your account:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>deletes your account, your sign-in and your profile (including your
      email address and display name) from our servers,</li>
      <li>revokes OurGarage's access to your Apple ID with Apple,</li>
      <li>if you were the only member of your household, deletes the household
      and everything shared in it &mdash; vehicles, service records, reminders,
      odometer readings, costs and notes &mdash; from our servers,</li>
      <li>if you owned a household that has other members, hands the household
      to the member who joined first, and removes you from it,</li>
      <li>if you were a member of someone else's household, removes you from it,</li>
      <li>if your purchase is what gave a household Premium, removes Premium from
      that household. Your purchase stays with your Apple ID and can be
      restored.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Shared vehicles and service history in a household that still has other
    members are <strong>not</strong> deleted, for the reason described above: they belong to
    the household, not only to you. Records you created there stay, but are no
    longer linked to you.</p>
    <p><strong>Everything stored on your phone stays on your phone</strong> after you delete
    your account, and you can keep using OurGarage without an account.
    Uninstalling the app removes it.</p>
    <p>Deleting your account does not cancel an App Store subscription. Manage or
    cancel it in your device's Settings &rarr; [your name] &rarr; Subscriptions.</p>
    <p>You can also ask us to delete your account by emailing
    <strong>support@noktastudio.dev</strong> from the address associated with it. We reply
    within 30 days, and typically much sooner.</p>
    <p>If you never created an account, there is nothing to delete on our end &mdash;
    uninstalling the app removes everything, since your data was never anywhere
    but your device.</p>

    <h2>Exporting your data</h2>
    <p>With OurGarage Premium you can export your records inside the app:
    Settings &rarr; <strong>Export records</strong> creates a CSV file of every vehicle and
    service record, or a PDF service history for one vehicle. The file is created
    on your device and goes only where you choose to share it; we never receive a
    copy. You can also email us for a copy of any personal data we hold about
    you (see below).</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Whether or not you are covered by a specific privacy law, you can email
    <strong>support@noktastudio.dev</strong> at any time to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>ask what personal data we hold about you,</li>
      <li>get a copy of it,</li>
      <li>correct anything that is wrong,</li>
      <li>have your account and personal data deleted (see above).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not require a reason, and we reply within 30 days.</p>
    <p>If you are located in the UK, EU, or EEA: our lawful basis for processing your
    data is performance of a contract (providing the household sharing you
    requested) and legitimate interests (operating and securing the service). You
    have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.</p>
    <p>If you are located in California: we do not sell or share personal
    information as defined by the CCPA, and we will not discriminate against you
    for exercising any right it grants you.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>OurGarage is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly
    collect personal data from anyone under that age. If you believe a child has
    provided us with personal data, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If we make a material change to this policy, we will update the date at the
    top of this page and, where the change is significant, notify you inside the
    app before it takes effect. We will never begin collecting a new category of
    data without updating this policy first.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><strong>support@noktastudio.dev</strong></p>
  </article>
</Base>
